abstract={In this article, we initiate the study of operator product expansions (OPEs) for the sine-Gordon model. For simplicity, we focus on the model below the first threshold of collapse ({\$}{\$}{\backslash}beta <4{\backslash}pi {\$}{\$}) and on the singular terms in OPEs of derivative-type fields {\$}{\$}{\backslash}partial {\backslash}varphi {\$}{\$}and {\$}{\$}{\backslash}bar{\{}{\backslash}partial {\}}{\backslash}varphi {\$}{\$}. We prove that compared to corresponding free field OPEs, the sine-Gordon OPEs develop logarithmic singularities and generate Wick ordered exponentials. Our approach for proving the OPEs relies heavily on Onsager-type inequalities and associated moment bounds for GFF correlation functions involving Wick ordered exponentials of the free field.},
